            <ArticleTitle>A fracture of unilateral pars interarticularis of the axis: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To present a case of a fracture of the unilateral pars interarticularis of the C2.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">There is confusion in the use of anatomic terminology of the pars interarticularis and pedicle of the C2 in literature. A fracture of the unilateral pars interarticularis of the C2 was diagnosed and treated nonsurgically by a Philadelphia collar.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The patient was free of pain and obtained a full range of motion.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The presumed mechanism of injury in the fracture described here was hyperextension and axial loading.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
